	regionKind = "world",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Azeroth is the world. Its seas hold the continents of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}, {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and frozen Northrend, and countless isles besides. Jungles, deserts, forests and fields of ice lie side by side across it, and in every land the ruins of older ages rest beneath the towns of the new. It is a world of many peoples and of very long memory. Again and again it has been made to bleed by powers that covet it, and again and again it has endured.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The oldest histories say that Azeroth was shaped by the titans, godlike beings who journeyed among the stars to bring order to the worlds they found. When they came to Azeroth, it was ruled by raging elementals and by ancient evils that had fastened themselves upon the world. The chronicles name these evils the Old Gods. The titans broke the power of both. They bound the elemental lords within a realm set apart from the world, and they imprisoned the Old Gods deep beneath the earth, for they could not be slain without wounding the world itself. Then the titans shaped the land. Their servants raised the mountains, carved the valleys and filled the seas. The earthen, beings of living stone, were set to tend the deep places of the world. Among the dragons, the titans chose five and gave each a share of their power. These became the Aspects, charged to guard Azeroth when its makers were gone. Then the titans departed, and the world was left to its own peoples.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Ages of the World",
			text = [=[• {b}The Kaldorei Empire.{/b} At the heart of a single great continent lay the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. On its shores the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} raised an empire of wonders under {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}.
• {b}The War of the Ancients.{/b} The reckless magic of the Highborne drew the eye of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. In the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, the night elves fought for the survival of the world, and the destruction of the Well brought about the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}. The one continent was broken into many.
• {b}The Younger Races.{/b} In the ages that followed, the troll empires waned and the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} awoke beneath the mountains. The {link:high-elves}high elves{/link} founded {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, and the {link:humans}human{/link} tribes united as {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} to fight the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}.
• {b}The Age of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} When the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened, the {link:orcs}orcs{/link} of another world poured into Azeroth. The {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} and the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} followed, each more terrible than the last.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "A Shared Name",
			text = [=[The name Azeroth once belonged to a human kingdom as well. The {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} exiles who settled the southern forests called their new realm Azeroth, and its capital was {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. In time the realm came to be known by the name of its city, and today it is the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Old soldiers of the {link:first-war}First War{/link} still sometimes speak of "Azeroth" and mean only the kingdom they lost.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:third-war}Third War{/link} ended with the fall of {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} at the foot of {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}, but it did not bring peace. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds the north of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Servants of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} still haunt the forests of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, who stood together on {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, now watch one another with suspicion across the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} and the woods of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}. Beneath {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}, the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron Dwarves{/link} serve a lord of living fire. Azeroth has survived every war yet fought upon it. No chronicler would dare to say that it cannot fall.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
