	regionKind = "continent",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Eastern Kingdoms stretch from the frozen peaks of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} to the jungles of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn{/link}. They are the homeland of {link:humans}humankind{/link}, of the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} and {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link}, and of the {link:high-elves}high elves{/link} of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}. Here stood the great human kingdoms of old, and here the {link:horde}Horde{/link} made its first war upon {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. The lands bear the scars of every war since. Once-proud realms lie in ruin, and the north has become a land of the dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, these lands were the eastern reaches of a single continent. When the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} was destroyed, the seas rushed in and tore them away. What remained was a land already old. The titans had left their works here, among them {link:uldaman}the vault of Uldaman{/link} in the stony {link:badlands}Badlands{/link}. Their earthen servants slept in its halls. Over long ages the earthen changed. Their flesh softened and their lives grew short, and from them came the dwarves of Khaz Modan. Another titan-forged people, it is written, gave rise to the gnomes. The trolls were older still in these lands. The Amani ruled the northern forests, and the Gurubashi held the southern jungles.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Coming of the Elves.{/b} Exiled from {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, the Highborne crossed the sea and founded {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} in the northern forests, upon lands the Amani claimed as their own.
• {b}Arathor.{/b} The human tribes of the north were united by {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, who raised the city of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. Together with the elves, his armies broke the Amani in the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}. In return the elves taught humans the ways of {link:arathor}Arathi{/link} magic, and Dalaran was later founded by the mages of that line.
• {b}The Seven Kingdoms.{/b} In time Arathor divided. The kingdoms of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}, {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}, {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} and Stromgarde rose in the north. In the south, {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} exiles founded the realm that became the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}.
• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} Beneath the mountains, the dwarves of {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Ironforge{/link} split into the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans. Their war ended in fire. The Dark Iron sorcerer-thane {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} called forth Ragnaros, lord of fire, and the summoning raised {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} and scorched the lands around it.
• {b}The Wars of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} The {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened in the south. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} fell in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} of Lordaeron threw back the Horde in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. Then came the plague of undeath, the {link:culling-of-stratholme}Culling of Stratholme{/link} and the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} has risen again, though its king is missing and its regent, {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link}, holds a realm stretched thin. {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link} rules in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, which also shelters the gnomes, for {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} has been lost to its own ruin. North of the {link:thandol-span}Thandol Span{/link}, the great kingdom of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} is no more. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds the Plaguelands. The zealots of the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} fight it with fire and suspicion alike. In the ruins of the old capital, the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} have made a home beneath the earth. In {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}, Dark Iron and {link:orcs}orc{/link} wage war on each other. And in the south, the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} stands silent in the {link:blasted-lands}Blasted Lands{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	id = "kalimdor",
	title = "Kalimdor",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "always" },
	},
	regionKind = "continent",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Kalimdor lies across the sea to the west of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. It is a land of old forests and red canyons, of great plains and burning deserts. It is the homeland of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} and the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, and the ancient heart of the world. The Kalimdor of today is only what survived the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}. Before that cataclysm, a single continent held nearly all the lands of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, and the lake at its center was the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The oldest peoples of Kalimdor were the trolls, whose empires spread far across the primordial continent. A tribe of trolls who settled beside the Well was changed by its power over many generations. They became the night elves, who named the land Kalimdor. Beside the Well they built the cities of the Kaldorei Empire under {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}. Their pursuit of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link} drew the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} into the world. In the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link} the Well was destroyed, and the continent was shattered. The seas poured into the wound, and the Maelstrom has churned there ever since. Upon the slopes of {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, the survivors planted {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}, and for ten thousand years the night elves kept a hidden vigil over their forests.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Long Vigil.{/b} Under {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} and {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link}, the night elves forswore arcane magic. The druids slept in the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, and the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} guarded the forests alone.
• {b}The Peoples of the Wilds.{/b} Across the plains roamed the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}. They were beset for generations by the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} of the south, the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} of the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}, the {link:harpies}harpies{/link} of the cliffs and the {link:furbolgs}furbolgs{/link} of the forests.
• {b}The Third War.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, a new {link:horde}Horde{/link} under {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} crossed the sea, and so did the humans of {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link}. The {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} followed them. Orc, human and {link:night-elves}night elf{/link}, once strangers and foes, stood together at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, and there {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} was destroyed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Kalimdor is no longer a hidden land. The night elves have planted a new tree, {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}, and its city of {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} looks out over the northern sea. The orcs have founded {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} and the city of {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}, and the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} have made {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} their home in {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}. The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear trolls{/link} dwell beside the orcs. {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} holds {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} in {link:dustwallow-marsh}Dustwallow Marsh{/link}. Yet the peace of Hyjal is fraying. Orc loggers cut the trees of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, and the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} answer with arrows. Goblins of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link} and the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} trade and plunder along the coasts. The forests of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link} still bear the taint of the Legion, and older mysteries sleep in the deserts of the south.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "war-of-the-ancients",
	title = "War of the Ancients",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The War of the Ancients was the first invasion of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} by the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. It was fought some ten thousand years before the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened, and it ended the Kaldorei Empire. Its last hour brought the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, which broke the world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Highborne of the {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} court drew ever deeper upon the power of the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. Their magic was felt beyond the world by {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}, the fallen titan who leads the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. He whispered to {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link}, and she believed him. {link:azshara}Azshara{/link} and her Highborne worked to open a gateway in the Well, so that Sargeras and his demons could enter {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The first demons came through, led by {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} and {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and they slaughtered the night elves who stood in their path. A resistance formed against them and against the queen. It was led by {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, a young student of the demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}, together with the priestess {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} and Malfurion's twin brother {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link}. The demigods of the wilds and the dragonflights joined the fight. The war was nearly lost when the Earth-Warder of the dragons betrayed his kind. He was the Aspect who would become {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link}. In the end the defenders reached the Highborne's palace and broke their spells as {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} tried to pass through. The gateway collapsed, and the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} tore itself apart.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[The war taught the night elves that arcane magic had nearly doomed the world. They forswore it, turned to druidism and the worship of Elune, and began their long vigil. It also left {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan{/link} a traitor in the eyes of his people, for he had worked with the Highborne in secret, and afterwards he made a new Well atop {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "great-sundering",
	title = "Great Sundering",
	aliases = { "Sundering" },
	category = "event",
