		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Great Sundering was the cataclysm that ended the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}. When the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} collapsed, the single continent of the ancient world was shattered, and the seas rushed in to fill the wound. The face of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} was changed forever.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The gateway of the Highborne was undone in the war's final hour. The Well, fed with more power than it could hold, imploded. The explosion tore the heart out of the continent. Most of the Kaldorei Empire, with its shining capital of Zin-Azshari, was swallowed by the sea. {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} and many of her Highborne were dragged beneath the waves. Where the Well had been, the waters began to spin, and the great storm known as the Maelstrom was born. It has never ceased.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The World After",
			text = [=[Only fragments of the old continent remained above the water. The largest of these became {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} in the west and the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link} in the east, and the frozen land of Northrend lay to the north. The surviving night elves gathered on the slopes of {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}. There they found that {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} had carried vials of the Well's water and poured them into a mountain lake, making a second Well. To guard it, the Aspects planted {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link} above its waters.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[For the night elves, the Sundering was proof of the cost of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link}. For the world, it meant ten thousand years of separation. The peoples of the east and the west forgot each other until the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} brought them together again. The {link:naga}naga{/link} who haunt the coasts today are said to be the drowned Highborne, changed beyond recognition.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "troll-wars",
	title = "Troll Wars",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Troll Wars were fought between the Amani trolls and the young kingdoms of humans and {link:high-elves}high elves{/link}, some two thousand eight hundred years before the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened. From them came the alliance of elves and humans, and the first human mages.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Highborne exiled from {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} founded {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} in the northern forests of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. Those forests had belonged to the Amani, and the trolls never forgave the theft. They made war on the elves for thousands of years. At last they gathered a great host, perhaps joined by their Gurubashi kin, and set out to destroy Quel'Thalas altogether.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[In the same age, {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link} of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} tribe had united the human tribes of the north into the nation of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}, with its capital at {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. The elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} sent envoys to him in desperation. Thoradin agreed to aid them if the elves would teach his people magic. The elves chose one hundred humans with a gift for the art and taught them only what was needed. The allied armies met the Amani host in the south of the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}. The human mages and elven magisters called down fire upon the trolls, and the flames burned away the wounds that trolls can otherwise heal. The Amani broke and fled, and their empire never recovered.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[In gratitude, the elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} swore an oath of friendship to the line of {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}. That oath would bring them into the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. The magic taught to humankind spread far beyond the first hundred. It gave rise to {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} and to the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link}, and it drew the notice of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} once more.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "first-war",
	title = "First War",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The First War was the invasion of the human kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} by the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link}. It began when the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened in the Black Morass, and it ended with the fall of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. It was the first war of {link:orcs}orc{/link} and human, and the beginning of the age that has shaped the world ever since.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[On their world of Draenor, the {link:orcs}orcs{/link} had been corrupted by the demon lord {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} through the warlock {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} and his {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}. Their homeland was dying. In {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, the Guardian of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, had long been possessed by the spirit of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}. Working with Gul'dan, Medivh helped open a gateway between the two worlds.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The first orcs came through in small numbers and raided the Black Morass. Then the portal widened and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} came in strength, under the warchief Blackhand. King {link:llane-wrynn}Llane Wrynn{/link} and his champion {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} fought them for years across the southern kingdom. The Horde burned the farms of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, the forests of {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link} and {link:northshire-abbey}Northshire Abbey{/link}. Lothar and the young mage {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link} at last slew the mad Guardian in his tower of {link:karazhan}Karazhan{/link}. It was too late for the kingdom. The half-{link:orcs}orc{/link} {link:garona}Garona{/link} slew King Llane in his own keep, {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} took the Horde from Blackhand, and {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} was sacked.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[{link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link} led the survivors north across the sea to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, taking with him {link:llane-wrynn}Llane{/link}'s son {link:varian-wrynn}Varian{/link}. Their warnings led King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} to gather the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and prepare for the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "second-war",
	title = "Second War",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Second War was fought between the {link:horde}Horde{/link} under {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. The Horde marched north to conquer the human kingdoms that survived the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. It was broken at {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} Spire.]=],
