		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} gathered the human kingdoms into an {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}, with {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} as its commander. The dwarves of {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and the gnomes joined them. So did the elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, bound by the old oath they had sworn to the line of {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, for Lothar was its last heir. The {link:horde}Horde{/link} came in greater strength than before. Doomhammer brought ogres and the Amani trolls of Zul'jin to his side. The {link:dragonmaw-clan}Dragonmaw clan{/link} enslaved the red dragonflight and rode its dragons into battle. {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} raised death knights from the corpses of fallen human knights. The Horde overran Khaz Modan and burned the borders of Quel'Thalas. Lord Perenolde of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} betrayed the Alliance to the orcs. The Horde reached the walls of the Lordaeron capital itself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Turning of the War",
			text = [=[At the height of the war, {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} abandoned Doomhammer. He sailed away with his followers to seek the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}, and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} was forced to turn back to punish him. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} seized the moment. It drove the Horde south to {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} Spire. There {link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link} fell to Doomhammer's hand. His lieutenant {link:turalyon}Turalyon{/link} took up his banner and crushed the Horde in the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[The surviving orcs were herded into internment camps. The {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} was destroyed. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} had won, but its victory was costly. Its kingdoms soon quarrelled over the price of the camps, and {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link} and {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} left the Alliance.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "third-war",
	title = "Third War",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Third War was the second invasion of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} by the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. It began in {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} with a plague of undeath and ended in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} with the destruction of {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}. It cost humankind its greatest kingdom and the night elves their immortality.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the demon {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} bound the spirit of the {link:orcs}orc{/link} shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link} in a frozen prison in Northrend and made him the Lich King. Through the necromancer {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} and his {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}, the Lich King spread a plague through the villages of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Its victims rose as the undead {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. At the same time, the young orc {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} freed his people from the internment camps and forged a new {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[A mysterious prophet warned the kings of the east to flee west across the sea. King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} would not listen, but {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} and {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} heeded the call. The prophet was {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, returned from death. In {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} hunted the plague to its source. After the {link:culling-of-stratholme}Culling of Stratholme{/link} he sailed to Northrend and took up the cursed blade Frostmourne. He returned as a death knight and brought about the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} raised {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} at the Sunwell of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, and {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} entered the world at {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} and destroyed it. Then the Legion followed the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and the humans into {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. There the night elves rose from their vigil.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[{link:orcs}Orcs{/link}, humans and night elves at last made common cause. At the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link} they destroyed {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}. From the war came the new {link:horde}Horde{/link}'s lands in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, the city of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} and the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. Its wounds are still open.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "battle-of-mount-hyjal",
	title = "Battle of Mount Hyjal",
	aliases = { "Battle of Hyjal" },
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Battle of Mount Hyjal was the last battle of the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. On the slopes of the sacred mountain, orcs, humans and night elves stood together against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. The demon lord {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} was destroyed at the roots of {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Legion had come to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} for the World Tree. {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} meant to drain the power of the second {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} that lay beneath its roots, and by doing so to consume the world. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} marched before him. The night elves of {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} and {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} could not stand alone. {link:medivh}Medivh{/link} brought together their leaders, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} of the humans. He told them that only together could they survive.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[{link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} devised the plan. The humans made their stand on the lower slopes, then the orcs higher up, and each held as long as they could before falling back. While they fought, Malfurion prepared a trap at the summit. {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} broke through each line in turn and at last reached the tree. As he climbed {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}, Malfurion sounded the Horn of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}. The spirits of the night elves' ancestors, gathered as countless wisps, swarmed upon the demon. Their power, and the power of the World Tree, was released in a single blast. Archimonde was destroyed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[The victory saved the world, but it came at a great price. {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link} gave up its power, and the night elves lost the immortality it had granted them. The tree was scorched but not slain. The battle also forged a brief peace between the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "culling-of-stratholme",
	title = "Culling of Stratholme",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Culling of Stratholme was the slaughter of the people of Stratholme by the soldiers of Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link}. It happened in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, when the plague of undeath reached the city. It marked the beginning of the prince's fall.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[{link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} had hunted the plague across {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} with the sorceress {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} and his mentor {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link}. He learned that the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} had tainted the grain shipped from the granaries of {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}. At Stratholme he found that the tainted grain had already been given out. Everyone who had eaten it would soon die and rise again as one of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[{link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} ordered the city purged before its people could turn. {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther{/link} refused to take part, and Arthas stripped him of his command for treason. {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina{/link} would not watch, and she left him. The prince led the soldiers who stayed loyal into Stratholme and put its people to the sword, house by house. Where they had not yet been reached, citizens were already turning. The dreadlord Mal'Ganis was waiting in the city. He mocked the prince and challenged him to follow to Northrend. Arthas swore to hunt him down.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[The Culling broke the bond between {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} and those who loved him. It sent him north, to Frostmourne and to the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Stratholme lies in ruins in the {link:eastern-plaguelands}Eastern Plaguelands{/link}. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds much of the city. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} clings to the rest, still fighting the dead that {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link}'s sword could not save.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "fall-of-lordaeron",
	title = "Fall of Lordaeron",
	category = "event",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Fall of Lordaeron was the ruin of the greatest human kingdom by the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. It came in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, when Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} returned from Northrend as the servant of the Lich King. Of all the kingdoms that had led the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}, none fell so far or so fast.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[In Northrend, {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} took up the runeblade Frostmourne and slew the dreadlord Mal'Ganis. He lost his soul to the blade. He sailed home, and the people of the capital greeted him as a hero. He walked into the throne room and slew his father, King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link}. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} swept over the kingdom behind him. Arthas killed {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link} and took the ashes of his father's urn, so that the remains of {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} could be carried in it. He marched into {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, cut down its defenders under {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}, and raised Kel'Thuzad in the waters of the Sunwell. Soon after, the Scourge helped {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} enter the world at {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "After the Fall",
			text = [=[When {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} was destroyed, the dreadlords sought to rule the ruined kingdom themselves. {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} turned against them before he answered his master's call to the north. {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link}, now undead, broke free of the Lich King's will. She and her {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} cast down the dreadlords and claimed the ruins of the capital.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} is gone. Its heartland is the Plaguelands, held by the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} fights the dead in {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link} and beyond. Beneath the broken throne room, the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} have built the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "dark-portal",
	title = "Dark Portal",
	category = "structure",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Dark Portal is the great gateway between {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} and the {link:orcs}orc{/link} homeland of Draenor. It stands in the {link:blasted-lands}Blasted Lands{/link}, which were once the swamps of the Black Morass. Through it came the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and with it began the {link:first-war}First War{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The portal was opened by the warlock {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} and his {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} from Draenor, with the help of {link:medivh}Medivh{/link} on {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. Medivh was the Guardian of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, but his mind had long been held by {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}, lord of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. At first the rift was narrow, and only a few scouts passed through. Then it was widened, and the whole {link:horde}Horde{/link} crossed into the swamp.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The {link:horde}Horde{/link} built a great fortress around the portal, and it became their road for reinforcements. When the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} was lost, the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} destroyed the Dark Portal. Some years later, the shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link} opened it again and led a new Horde through to steal artifacts of power. The Alliance sent an expedition across into Draenor to end the threat at its source. Ner'zhul tore open rifts to other worlds, and the portal was destroyed again. The expedition did not return. None in {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} know what became of it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Dark Portal stands dark and silent at the southern end of the {link:blasted-lands}Blasted Lands{/link}. The mages and soldiers of {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link} watch over it. Demons still roam the barren land around it.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "well-of-eternity",
	title = "Well of Eternity",
	category = "structure",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Well of Eternity was a vast lake of arcane power at the heart of the ancient world. On its shores the Kaldorei Empire rose. Its destruction ended the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link} and caused the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[The oldest histories say that the Well filled a wound in the earth, left by the titans' war upon the Old Gods. Its waters were black and deep, and they held the raw power of the world itself. The trolls who settled near it were changed over many generations, and they became the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}. They learned to wield its power, and their mastery of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link} made their empire the wonder of the world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} queen {link:queen-azshara}Azshara{/link} built her palace on the Well's shores, and her Highborne drew upon it ever more deeply. Their magic drew the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. The Highborne tried to open a gateway for {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} within the Well itself. When the gateway was undone, the Well collapsed, and the continent was torn apart. Where it had been, the Maelstrom now rages.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Its Legacy",
			text = [=[Something of the Well survived. {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} saved vials of its waters and poured them into a lake on {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, making a second Well. There the Aspects planted {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}. The exiled Highborne carried another vial east. With it they made the Sunwell, the fount of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} to consume the power of the second Well, and he failed.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "nordrassil",
	title = "Nordrassil",
	category = "structure",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Nordrassil is the World Tree, which rises from the summit of {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link} in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. For ten thousand years it guarded the second {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} and gave the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} their immortality. It was the center of the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, the surviving night elves found that {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} had made a new Well atop {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}. The dragon Aspects came to them. {link:alexstrasza}Alexstrasza{/link} placed a sacred seed in the waters of the new Well, and a great tree rose from it, its roots drinking from the Well and sealing it away. Nozdormu blessed the tree so that the night elves would live as long as it stood. Ysera bound it to the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, so that the druids might walk the Dream through it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[Under its boughs the night elves kept their long vigil. The druids of {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} slept in its shadow, their spirits wandering the Dream. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} marched on the tree to drain the Well beneath it. As he climbed its trunk, Malfurion called the spirits of the ancestors, and the power of Nordrassil was spent in destroying the demon.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Nordrassil still stands, scarred and weakened. The night elves are no longer immortal. They have planted a new tree, {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}, off the northern coast, but it was grown without the blessing of the Aspects. Many of the old druids doubt whether it should have been grown at all.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "holy-light",
	title = "Holy Light",
	category = "force",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Holy Light is the power of faith and virtue that answers the devoted. Its priests heal wounds and mend spirits. Its paladins bear it into battle as a shield and a weapon against the undead and the demonic. Most humans of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link} have been raised in its faith, and many {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} now share it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[The faithful do not teach that the Light is a god. They teach that it dwells within all who strive for virtue, and that it grows stronger through compassion, courage and sacrifice. It cannot be stolen or bent to cruelty. Those who try to wield it without faith find that it does not answer them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The faith of the Light has deep roots among humankind, reaching back to the days of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}. In the kingdom of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} it was kept at {link:northshire-abbey}Northshire Abbey{/link} and in the {link:cathedral-of-light}Cathedral of Light{/link}. After the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, Archbishop {link:alonsus-faol}Alonsus Faol{/link} saw that faith alone had not saved the south. He joined the clerics of the Light with the finest knights of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} and founded the Order of the Silver Hand, the first paladins. {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link} was the first of them. The paladins fought with honor through the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the order was torn apart. Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} had been one of them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Light is still the heart of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}'s faith, and its priests serve in every town. In {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, it has become a battle cry. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} burns all it suspects of the plague in the Light's name. The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} fights the same dead with a steadier hand.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "arcane-magic",
	title = "Arcane Magic",
	category = "force",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Arcane magic is the magic of the mind and of the patterns of the world. Its masters bend space and time, summon fire and frost, and see what others cannot. It is the oldest learned magic of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, and the most dangerous to those who love it too much.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[Arcane power can be learned by those with talent and discipline, but it gives nothing for free. Those who wield it grow to crave it. It also calls to the demons of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}, who hunger for worlds rich in magic. Every great age of arcane power in {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} has drawn the Legion's eye.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The night elves first mastered arcane magic at the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}, and their Highborne used it to bring about the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}. After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, the night elves outlawed it. The Highborne who would not give it up were exiled. They founded {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} in the east and became the {link:high-elves}high elves{/link}. In the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link} they taught magic to one hundred humans of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}. The art spread through human lands. The mages of Arathor raised the city of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}, and its ruling council, the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link}, watched over the use of magic. When demons began to appear in human lands, the elves and the mages founded the secret Council of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}. They chose a Guardian to fight the Legion alone. The last Guardians were {link:aegwynn}Aegwynn{/link} and her son {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} was destroyed by {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. Now its mages rebuild it behind a shimmering violet barrier in the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} foothills. Magi still train in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}. Among the night elves, the old law against arcane magic stands.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "fel-magic",
	title = "Fel Magic",
	category = "force",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Fel magic is the magic of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. It draws its power from destruction and from the theft of life. It burns with a sickly green fire, and it poisons the land and the souls of those who use it. Warlocks still bargain with it, knowing the price.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[Fel power is quick and strong, and it asks for little study. It asks instead for something to be consumed: a life, a soul, the health of the land. Those who use it are slowly changed, in body and in heart. Places where it has been used often wither and rot.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[Fel magic first came to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} with the Legion in the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}. Many Highborne who served the demons were twisted into {link:satyrs}satyrs{/link}. Ten thousand years later, it came again through the {link:orcs}orcs{/link}. On Draenor, the demon lord {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} taught its secrets to {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} and his warlocks. The orc chieftains drank the blood of the demon {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and it filled them with a terrible rage. The land of Draenor died beneath their magic. The orcs carried the curse through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} into the {link:first-war}First War{/link} and the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:grom-hellscream}Grom Hellscream{/link} slew Mannoroth and freed his people from the demon's blood at the cost of his own life. {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} consumed the {link:skull-of-gul-dan}Skull of Gul'dan{/link} and took on a demon's power.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The forests of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link} still bear the taint of the Legion. The warlocks of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} serve demons in the shadows of {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} and {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}. The satyrs haunt {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}. Warlocks of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} still study the art. They insist that they are its masters.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "emerald-dream",
	title = "Emerald Dream",
	category = "force",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Emerald Dream is a vast spirit realm that mirrors the world. It shows {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} as it might have been, wild and untouched by the hands of mortals. Its guardian is Ysera, the Aspect of the green dragonflight. The druids of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} walk it in spirit while their bodies sleep.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[The chronicles hold that the titans shaped the Dream as a living image of their design for the world. It is the realm of growth and of dreams. The green dragons guard its gates, and the spirits of the wild dwell within it. Time and distance there do not follow the rules of the waking world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[The demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} taught {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} the ways of druidism, and through them Malfurion learned to enter the Dream. After the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, Ysera bound {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link} to the Dream. For thousands of years, the druids of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} slept in hidden barrows, their spirits wandering the Dream while the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} guarded their bodies. They were woken to fight in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. After the victory, the druids returned to their work.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} has gone into the Dream once more, and he has not returned. {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} leads the druids in his absence. Something is wrong within the Dream. Green dragons are seen in the waking world, and some of them are no longer what they were. The druids of {link:moonglade}Moonglade{/link} speak of a darkness spreading through the Dream, which none can yet name.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "elements",
	title = "Elements",
	category = "force",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The elements are the living forces of earth, fire, water and air. In their raw forms they are wild and destructive. In balance they sustain the world. The shamans of the {link:orcs}orcs{/link}, the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and the {link:trolls}trolls{/link} speak with the spirits of the elements and ask for their aid.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature",
			text = [=[Four great elemental lords rule the elements. Ragnaros is lord of fire. Therazane is mother of stone. {link:al-akir}Al'Akir{/link} is lord of the winds, whose realm is {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}. Neptulon is lord of the tides. Their servants are wild and hostile to mortal life. The lesser spirits, however, can be reasoned with. A shaman does not command them. A shaman asks, and the spirits choose whether to answer.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[In the first age of the world, the elemental lords fought for the Old Gods. The titans defeated them and bound them in a realm apart from the world. On Draenor, the orcs were a people of shamans. When {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} turned them to demon magic, the spirits abandoned them. Far later, in Khaz Modan, the Dark Iron thane {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} summoned Ragnaros into the world. The summoning killed the thane and raised {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}. Ragnaros has dwelled beneath it ever since. After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the old shaman {link:drek-thar}Drek'Thar{/link} taught the ways of the spirits to young {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}. The elements answered the new {link:horde}Horde{/link} as they had not answered the old.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Ragnaros rules the Dark Iron dwarves from the molten depths of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}. The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} seeks to wake the elements for its own ends. Shamans of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} keep the old balance, as their ancestors did before the demons came.]=],
		},
	},
})
